# docs/ci-guide.md documents the blueprint-result.json schema with a real
# example finding whose rule_id ("secret:hardcoded-secret") legitimately trips
# kern's TOKEN detector. The file is documentation of the artifact schema, not
# source; excluding it keeps the doc's truthful example intact. Other docs
# remain scanned.
docs/ci-guide.md

# gitleaks/check.go contains rule-ID strings like "secret:incumbent-unavailable"
# that trip kern's TOKEN detector. This is source code referencing rule IDs, not
# actual secrets.
internal/blueprint/adapters/gitleaks/check.go

# Action README contains @v0.1.0 version refs that trip kern's EMAIL detector.
.github/actions/blueprint-ci/README.md

# README.md documents the reusable action with an @v0.1.0 version ref (the
# first release tag); "blueprint-ci@v0.1.0" trips kern's EMAIL detector because
# the version part starts with a letter (v), which the version-like filter does
# not recognize. Documentation of the tag convention, not a secret.
README.md